---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { site } from "../site";

const officer = site.informationOfficer;
const deleteEmail = officer.email || site.email;
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How IsangoTech collects, uses and protects personal information under POPIA.">
  <Prose title="Privacy policy">
    <p>
      Version {site.privacyPolicyVersion}{site.privacyPolicyDate && `, ${site.privacyPolicyDate}`}. This policy explains
      how {site.name} handles your personal information under the Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA).
    </p>
    {
      site.legalName && (
        <p>
          {site.name} is {site.legalName}, a private company registered in South Africa
          {site.companyRegistrationNumber && ` (registration number ${site.companyRegistrationNumber})`}, based in East
          London. We are the responsible party for the personal information described here.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you contact us or fill in a form, we collect only what we need to help you:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name, business name and industry</li>
      <li>your phone number and, if you give it, your email address</li>
      <li>what you tell us about your business and what you need</li>
      <li>if you book an assessment, the time you picked</li>
      <li>your consent choices, when you gave them, and which version of this policy you agreed to</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>to reply to your enquiry and give you advice or a quote</li>
      <li>to arrange and carry out an assessment you booked</li>
      <li>to message you on WhatsApp, only if you said we may</li>
      <li>if you become a client, to deliver our services, invoice you and support you</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell your information, and we don't use it for anything you haven't agreed to.</p>

    <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
    <p>
      Our systems run on Supabase, which stores data in data centres in the European Union or the United Kingdom,
      because it has no South African region. That means your information is transferred outside South Africa. We only
      use providers bound by a data processing agreement that protects your information to a standard at least as high
      as POPIA requires.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      If you don't become a client, we anonymise your details after 12 months without contact. If you do become a
      client, we keep your records for as long as we work together and as long as the law requires for financial
      records afterwards.
    </p>

    <h2>How we protect it</h2>
    <p>
      Only our staff can see your information. Each person signs in with their own password, with the option of a
      second check on their phone, and sees only what their work needs. We keep a record of who changes or exports information, and access is
      removed the day someone leaves.
    </p>

    <h2 id="whatsapp-assistant">The WhatsApp Assistant</h2>
    <p>
      Some of our clients use our WhatsApp Assistant to answer their customers and take bookings. If you message one of
      those businesses on WhatsApp, the business is the responsible party for your information and we process it on its
      behalf, only to provide the service it asked for.
    </p>
    <p>To do that we receive, through WhatsApp's own Business Platform (run by Meta):</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your WhatsApp number and the name on your WhatsApp profile</li>
      <li>the messages you send the business, and the replies sent to you</li>
      <li>any bookings you make, change or cancel</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use this only to reply to you, manage your bookings and send the reminders you agreed to. Your messages are
      passed to an AI model (through OpenRouter, which connects us to providers such as Anthropic) to write the
      Assistant's replies. Those providers may process data outside South Africa, and we use them only on terms that
      stop them keeping your messages or training their models on them. We never sell this information, use it for
      advertising, or share it with any business other than the one you messaged.
    </p>
    <p>
      Chat messages are deleted automatically after the period the business chooses, 12 months unless it sets a shorter
      one. Bookings are kept as part of the business's records.
    </p>

    <h2 id="delete-your-data">Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      To have your information deleted, email <a href={`mailto:${deleteEmail}`}>{deleteEmail}</a> from your own address,
      or send a WhatsApp message to the business you dealt with, saying "Delete my data". Tell us the phone number you
      used. We'll confirm who you are, delete your messages, contact details and bookings (or remove your name and number
      from records the business must keep by law, such as invoices), and confirm in writing within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us at any time to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>tell you what information we hold about you</li>
      <li>correct it or delete it</li>
      <li>stop contacting you on WhatsApp or for marketing</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      {
        officer.name ? (
          <>
            Contact our Information Officer, {officer.name}, at <a href={`mailto:${officer.email}`}>{officer.email}</a>.
          </>
        ) : (
          <>Contact us using the details on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</>
        )
      }
      If you're not happy with our response, you can complain to the Information Regulator at
      <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za">inforegulator.org.za</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
    <p>
      If we ever discover that your information has been accessed without permission, we'll contain it, assess it, and
      notify you and the Information Regulator as POPIA requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This website doesn't use tracking or advertising cookies, and our fonts are served from our own site. Our spam
      check (Cloudflare Turnstile) runs only on our forms, to tell people from bots. The map on our contact page loads
      from Google, which may set cookies, only if you choose to show it.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
